      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the next few days, closely monitor the incision site for signs of infection, such as excessive redness, swelling, pus, or foul odor. Also, watch for systemic signs of infection like fever or lethargy. Generally, you can start offering feed slowly and gradually, often starting with small amounts of easily digestible forage or hay as advised by your veterinarian. Always follow your vet's specific instructions regarding diet progression after surgery.",
